    "confers: catalog null -> the PARSE form (go ConfersAuthority(perms); ts confersAuthority({permissions}); java RolePredicates.confersAuthority(perms)).",
    "confers: catalog [] or a named catalog -> the CATALOG form (go ConfersAuthorityWithCatalog(perms, catalog); ts confersAuthority({permissions}, {catalog}); java RolePredicates.confersAuthority(perms, catalog)). An EMPTY catalog gives the parse-form answer.",
    "confers: permission strings are used exactly as given. No language trims, lowercases or otherwise rewrites them.",
    "assignable: go IsRoleAssignableTo(role, kind); ts isRoleSeatable(role, kind); java RolePredicates.isRoleAssignableTo(role, kind). 'role' uses the wire field names; an absent field takes the wire default (assignable_to absent = null).",
    "assignable: an empty or absent assignable_to admits ANY kind, as the issuer's realmrole.AssignableToKind does; a non-empty list admits only the kinds it names."
